  "synonym_discrimination": null,
  "usage_note": "**On** with a noun after it (*on the table*) is a preposition, in the entry **on** (preposition); **on** after **be** meaning *working* or *happening* (*The light is on*, *Is the party still on?*) is an adjective. Many phrasal verbs use **on**, such as **go on**, **carry on**, **get on**, and **turn on**; each has its own entry. *And so on* is in the entry for **and**.",
  "learner_errors": [
    {
      "incorrect": "I wore on my coat.",
      "correct": "I put on my coat.",
      "note": "**Put on** is the action of dressing; **wear** describes having clothes on, and takes no **on**: *I wore my coat*."
    },
    {
      "incorrect": "Please open the TV.",
      "correct": "Please turn the TV on.",
      "note": "A machine or a light is turned **on** or switched **on**; **open** is not used."
    }
  ],
